n       c0 = np.convolve(p0, p0, mode='full')\n       max_c0 = c0.max()\n       grad_part = (c0 - max_c0) / (max_c0 + 1e-10)   # saves computation and supports sparsity\n       grad_full = corr_weights(grad_part, p0)\n       return grad_full\n   ```\n\n   Implementation details:\n   - `evaluate_sequence` handles normalization, clipping, and convolution.\n   - We use exponential scaling to manage numerical stability.\n   - The optimization loop: 500 to 10,000 steps, dynamically resampling resolution.\n\n3. **Implementation procedure**:\n   We develop the `propose_candidate` function as follows:\n\n   ```python\n   def propose_candidate(budget=1800):\n       t0 = time.time()\n\n       # Step 1: Get initial sequence (normalized if parent is larger than 1)\n       n_init = 256\n       try:\n           if 'height_sequence_1' in globals():\n               parent = height_sequence_1.astype(np.float64)\n               if parent.size == n_init:\n                   seq_base = parent\n               elif parent.size < n_init:\n                   # Downscale parent if needed\n                   seq_base = interpolate_seq(parent, n_init)\n               else:\n                   # Stretch parent if necessary\n                   # Parent might have a different length than targeted 256\n                   seq_base = parent[:n_init] / parent[:n_init].sum()\n           else:\n               # Generate random seed\n               seq_base = np.random.uniform(0, 1000, size=n_init)\n               if seq_base.sum() < 0.01:\n                   seq_base = (seq_base + np.random.rand(n_init)/2).clip(0, 1000) / seq_base.sum()\n       except Exception as e:\n           print(f\"Using fallback: {e}\")\n           parent = np.random.uniform(0, 1, 100)\n           seq_base = make_linear_profile(n_init, 1.5)   # fallback\n\n       # Step 2: Define optimization parameters\n       beta_height = 1e-10  # small smoothing parameter to avoid extreme values\n       alpha = 0.3  # decay factor for expon